# 4. Scope of Fouling Modeling

This project must focus on **MINERAL SCALING ONLY**.

Do not develop independent organic-fouling, colloidal-fouling, biological-fouling, or combined-fouling modules.

Do not add these mechanisms merely to increase the dataset size.

They may be mentioned in the literature review and future-work section.

An additional mechanism may only be considered if you identify a directly relevant published mathematical model containing sufficiently specified equations, parameters, and validation evidence that can be transferred to this RED system.

If such evidence is not available, exclude the mechanism from implementation.

The principal mineral-scaling mechanisms are:

1. Calcium carbonate (CaCO3).
2. Gypsum (CaSO4·2H2O).

Silica may be studied as a separate published-performance benchmark if the experimental conditions can be reproduced, but do not automatically create an independent silica deposition-kinetics model.

Prioritize CaCO3 because Santoro et al. (2021) provide a RED-specific heterogeneous-nucleation model.

Treat gypsum as a second mineral of interest, using the 2026 RED study as a performance benchmark.

