3. Check electroneutrality.
4. Document missing analytical species.
5. Record the source of every concentration.
6. Check whether the membrane transport equations support each species.
7. Identify the activity-coefficient model used.

Do not automatically convert an incomplete brine profile into a fully specified electrolyte system by inventing missing concentrations.

